{
  "info": {
    "name": "University Record Service",
    "description": "University Record through the Gateway: base_url is {{gateway}}/api/v1/university-record. A player's request names the player in X-Player-Id, which the collection pre-request script turns into a signed Bearer JWT; a service's request carries X-Service-Token. Run the 'scenario' folder top to bottom.\n\nLAB 4 (4.0.0). applicant.initialized, session.started and session.ended arrive from the Message Broker (topics events.<event_type>), not on POST /events, which is removed; this service's own applicant.initialized is published to events.applicant.initialized. Postman cannot send the broker's gRPC calls: the events of the scenario have to be published to the broker with the full envelope first (docs/UNIVERSITY_RECORD_SERVICE.md, \u00a711), and the session's scopes are set with the session-service mock (POST /admin/sessions/{id}/scopes).\n\nDIRECT CALLS. GET /logs and GET /metrics are not Gateway routes: they go to one instance directly through {{university_record_direct_url}}. GET /logs needs {{service_token}}.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
